From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] prntvpt: a print ticket's own choices stand in the driver's devmode

Since 1031 a devmode made from a print ticket is the driver's whole
devmode (DocumentProperties merges the ticket's settings into the
driver's). The driver's merge put its nearest paper in place of a custom
size, so a label's custom width and length (DYMO Connect's) became the
driver's paper. The ticket's own public choices (orientation, paper or
custom size, copies, source, colour, duplex, collation, quality, media)
stand as it gives them now.

Test: test/usbprint-gate.sh (mutant SG_MUTANT_PTKEEPPUBLIC);
test/drvui-gate.sh still covers the driver's own settings in a ticket.
---
--- a/dlls/prntvpt/ticket.c
+++ b/dlls/prntvpt/ticket.c
@@ -1134,6 +1134,27 @@
         if (full >= (LONG)sizeof(pub) && (*dm = malloc(full)) &&
             DocumentPropertiesW(NULL, prov->hprn, prov->name, *dm, &pub, DM_IN_BUFFER | DM_OUT_BUFFER) == IDOK)
         {
+            /* the ticket's own choices stand as it gives them (a custom size
+             * stays a width and length, not the driver's nearest paper) */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_PTKEEPPUBLIC
+            if (pub.dmFields & DM_ORIENTATION) (*dm)->dmOrientation = pub.dmOrientation;
+            if (pub.dmFields & DM_PAPERSIZE) (*dm)->dmPaperSize = pub.dmPaperSize;
+            if (pub.dmFields & DM_PAPERLENGTH) (*dm)->dmPaperLength = pub.dmPaperLength;
+            if (pub.dmFields & DM_PAPERWIDTH) (*dm)->dmPaperWidth = pub.dmPaperWidth;
+            if (pub.dmFields & DM_COPIES) (*dm)->dmCopies = pub.dmCopies;
+            if (pub.dmFields & DM_DEFAULTSOURCE) (*dm)->dmDefaultSource = pub.dmDefaultSource;
+            if (pub.dmFields & DM_COLOR) (*dm)->dmColor = pub.dmColor;
+            if (pub.dmFields & DM_DUPLEX) (*dm)->dmDuplex = pub.dmDuplex;
+            if (pub.dmFields & DM_COLLATE) (*dm)->dmCollate = pub.dmCollate;
+            if (pub.dmFields & DM_PRINTQUALITY) (*dm)->dmPrintQuality = pub.dmPrintQuality;
+            if (pub.dmFields & DM_YRESOLUTION) (*dm)->dmYResolution = pub.dmYResolution;
+            if (pub.dmFields & DM_MEDIATYPE) (*dm)->dmMediaType = pub.dmMediaType;
+            if (!(pub.dmFields & DM_PAPERSIZE) && (pub.dmFields & (DM_PAPERLENGTH | DM_PAPERWIDTH)))
+                (*dm)->dmFields &= ~DM_PAPERSIZE;
+            (*dm)->dmFields |= pub.dmFields & (DM_ORIENTATION | DM_PAPERSIZE | DM_PAPERLENGTH | DM_PAPERWIDTH |
+                    DM_COPIES | DM_DEFAULTSOURCE | DM_COLOR | DM_DUPLEX | DM_COLLATE | DM_PRINTQUALITY |
+                    DM_YRESOLUTION | DM_MEDIATYPE);
+#endif
             for (i = 0; i < ticket.driver_count; i++)
                 driver_set_feature(prov->hprn, prov->name, *dm, ticket.driver[i].feature, ticket.driver[i].option);
             *size = (*dm)->dmSize + (*dm)->dmDriverExtra;
